WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.981
172 in binary is 10101100.

00:03.981 --> 00:14.700
Checking all eight bits works, but half of those checks land on zeros.

00:15.000 --> 00:21.123
Think of a row of light switches.

00:21.123 --> 00:31.700
One trick turns off only the rightmost switch that’s lit.

00:32.000 --> 00:38.978
Subtract one and the lowest 1 flips off.

00:38.978 --> 00:47.700
AND that with n, and only that one bit disappears.

00:48.000 --> 00:51.495
Four 1 bits, four hops.

00:51.495 --> 00:59.700
That’s O(k) for k one bits, and the zeros are skipped.
